            <ArticleTitle>Simultaneous subacute thrombosis of bare metal coronary stents in two different arteries early after clopidogrel cessation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>309-13</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary stent thrombosis is a rare event leading to ST segment elevation myocardial infarction and death. Although early thrombosis of drug-eluting and bare metal stents is relatively frequent, simultaneous thrombosis of bare metal coronary stents has rarely been reported. Here, we present a case of simultaneous subacute thrombosis of two bare metal stents in different coronary arteries early after clopidogrel cessation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
